 36S  c  1990Ho19: E=28.0 MeV proton and E=31.6 MeV |a beams were produced from 
 36S 2c  the AVF cyclotron of the Vrije Universiteit. Targets were enriched     
 36S 3c  sulphur. Reaction products were momentum analyzed with an Enge         
 36S 4c  split-pole magnetic spectrograph (FWHM=14 keV for proton and 24 keV for
 36S 5c  |a). Measured particle spectra, |s(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,         
 36S 6c  L-transfers, deformation lengths, and transition strenghts from        
 36S 7c  analysis of measured |s(|q) using DWBA calculations and couple-channel 
 36S 8c  calculations. Comparisons with shell-model and extended-RPA            
 36S 9c  calculations. See also 1989Ho14 from the same group                    
 36S  c  Mass deformation lengths are deduced from |s(|q) data in 1990Ho19 using
 36S 2c  phenomenological and folding analyses                                  
